/**
@page matlab_installation Installation

@section matlab_requirements Requirements

- MATLAB R2022b or later
- Java 8 or higher (for the JAR backend)

@section matlab_installing Installing LINE

Download the latest release from SourceForge.

To install LINE for MATLAB:

1. Download and extract the LINE package
2. Start MATLAB
3. Navigate to the `matlab` directory within the LINE project
4. Run the installation script:

@code{.m}
lineInstall
@endcode

This only needs to be done once. The installation script downloads required Java dependencies and configures the MATLAB path.

@section matlab_dependencies Dependencies

LINE for MATLAB requires the following Java dependencies (automatically downloaded by `lineInstall`):

- jline.jar (core LINE library)
- JMT.jar (Java Modelling Tools, for simulation)

These will be automatically downloaded when you run `lineInstall`.

@section matlab_starting Starting LINE

Before using LINE in a MATLAB session, you must first initialize it by running `lineStart`. This script adds the necessary LINE folders to the MATLAB path.

@code{.m}
lineStart
@endcode

You need to run `lineStart` at the beginning of each MATLAB session where you intend to use LINE.

@section matlab_verifying Verifying Installation

To verify your installation, run:

@code{.m}
lineStart
model = Network('Test');
disp('LINE installation successful!');
@endcode

*/
